## Connection

Connect the **{{name}}** integration with:

- **Base URL** — the API root, e.g. `https://api.example.com`.
- **API Token** — created in the provider's UI.

The credentials are stored in Sophon's credential vault and supplied to the skill at call time under
their exact manifest field keys (`baseUrl`, `apiToken`); they are never written into the skill.

## Development notes

- `main.py` runs at module scope with an injected `params` global — there is no stdin protocol and
  no `__main__` block.
- Read credentials at module scope; read tool arguments inside handlers. The build script uses that
  split to distinguish them.
- `credentials[].access` must be `"injected"`. `"proxy"` names an unimplemented broker and means the
  skill receives no credentials at all.
- Field keys are permanent: renaming one orphans every stored credential.

Add tests as `tests/skills/test_{{name}}.py` in this repo, using the `mockhttp` harness; run them
with `python tests/skills/run_all.py`.

